  "name": "IGG BY IMMUNOTURBIDMETRY",
  "code": "1118",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul>\n<li data-start=\"89\" data-end=\"236\">\n<p data-start=\"91\" data-end=\"236\">IgG (Immunoglobulin G) is the most abundant immunoglobulin in the serum and provides long-term protection by neutralizing pathogens and toxins.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"237\" data-end=\"330\">\n<p data-start=\"239\" data-end=\"330\">It plays a central role in humoral immunity and is crucial for secondary immune response.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"331\" data-end=\"497\">\n<p data-start=\"333\" data-end=\"497\">Quantification of IgG is important for evaluating immune status, diagnosing immunodeficiency disorders, and monitoring autoimmune or plasma cell-related diseases.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"498\" data-end=\"646\">\n<p data-start=\"500\" data-end=\"646\">It is frequently assessed in cases of recurrent infections, unexplained inflammation, monoclonal gammopathies, and suspected immunodeficiencies.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>IgG Level</th>\n<th>Possible Clinical Indications</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Elevated</td>\n<td>Chronic infections (e.g., tuberculosis), autoimmune diseases (e.g., SLE, rheumatoid arthritis), liver disease (e.g., cirrhosis), multiple myeloma (IgG type), monoclonal gammopathy (MGUS), chronic inflammation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Decreased</td>\n<td>Primary immunodeficiencies (e.g., common variable immunodeficiency, X-linked agammaglobulinemia), protein-losing conditions (e.g., nephrotic syndrome, protein-losing enteropathy), leukemia, immunosuppressive therapy</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
